  "subtitle-win": [
    "France and Spain sit at the front of the tightly bunched 2026 World Cup field due to their exceptional squad depth, recent continental success, and consistent results in qualifiers. Spain\u2019s long unbeaten streak and Euro 2024 title bolster their standing, while France\u2019s talent pool and tournament pedigree maintain near parity. England\u2019s reliability, Argentina\u2019s bid for back-to-back titles with its core intact, and Portugal\u2019s attacking options further compress probabilities among the leading contenders. The expanded 48-team format and challenging North American conditions add layers of unpredictability that traders price into this competitive opening."
  ],
  "subtitle-final": [
